From 56524162cc00dbbce8def381ba1b458af638aadb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:57:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] build: size short warning regressions accurately

Declare eleven measured short regression tests as small. Keep verbose
Bazel timeout diagnostics enabled and preserve every test assertion.

Red: hosted Linux musl execution reports oversized timeout declarations
for the two V8 action-analysis tests, both completing within 0.1 seconds.
The earlier nine regressions reproduce the same timing-range advisories.
Green: all nine original focused tests pass without timing advisories;
both V8 action-analysis tests pass in 0.0 seconds without advisories.
Fresh emitted-patch verification reruns all eleven tests, just fmt-check,
and just bazel-lock-check against rust-v0.162.1 with queue prerequisites.

Refs: https://github.com/holdmyspot-com/codex-unleashed/issues/61
